--TEST--
An object literal is refused where its `{` or one of its fields would have two meanings: at the start of a statement, directly after a closure's `=>`, on a local declaration typed with a bare shape, with a field written twice, with a required field missing, and with a field the shape types differently — `rule:types/shape-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/anonymous-objects
// A `{` opens a block before it is anything else, so the two positions
// where a statement could start take the parenthesised literal instead.
// Both are asked here: the bare statement, and the body of an arrow
// function, where the `=>` is followed by an expression and a reader would
// see a block. The local declaration is the third face of the same
// ambiguity, and `rule:types/shape-type` names the way out: the shape gets
// a name, and the declaration uses the name.
//
// The arrow function reports once. Its body is refused, and a refused
// expression reports no type mismatch of its own against `Point`.
//
// The three field diagnostics are what is left once the braces parse. A
// name written twice has no answer for which value the field takes. A
// missing required field and a field of another type are ordinary
// assignability against the shape, which is the whole of a shape's
// checking, so both name the literal's own shape and not the field alone.
type Point = {x: int, y: int};

Point $ordered = {x: 1, y: 2};

{x: 1};
callable(int): Point $make = fn(int $x): Point => {x: $x, y: 0};
{label: string} $bare = {label: "no name"};
Point $twice = {x: 1, x: 2, y: 3};
Point $short = {x: 1};
Point $typed = {x: 1, y: "two"};
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0117]: an anonymous object here is ambiguous with a block
%A
error[E0117]: an anonymous object here is ambiguous with a block
%A
error[E0134]: a local declaration cannot be typed with a bare shape
%A
error[E0494]: the field `x` is written twice in this anonymous object
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{x: int, y: int}`, found `{x: int}`
%A
error[E0401]: expected `{x: int, y: int}`, found `{x: int, y: string}`
%A
error: aborting due to 6 errors
